                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Last Berserker is a good mobile port with simple but addictive gameplay. It's much like One Finger Death Punch (one of my favorite games), but you can only take one hit and there's a meter which lets you know when you're about to be attacked. Dying feels like it's totally your fault and not because the game is unfair.\n\nIf you've played OFDP before, DO NOT use your mouse since it'll only attack the side you have your cursor on and more than likely you'll end up whiffing and dying. Instead you use the default \"A\" and \"D\" on your keyboard to attack. \n\nThe graphics are nice but there is only one music track which is tolerable and only five types of enemies. Red ones require two hits to defeat, the rest just one. There are a variety of fighters to unlock that are merely cosmetic (as far as I can tell at this point), but it's quite grindy to get a new one. Personally, that gives me more incentive to play. You can just get the DLC if you just want to have all the characters at once, but it isn't necessary.\n\nOverall, it's a worthy purchase if you want some quick fun and to support a non-crappy reflex fighter.",
